      "mechanism": "The patch changes the reset value of input_axis_tready_reg from 0 to hold its previous value (input_axis_tready_reg). At cycle 8, the FSM is in STATE_IDLE with EXPAND_BUS=1 and CYCLE_COUNT=8. The original code unconditionally sets input_axis_tready_next=1 in STATE_IDLE when EXPAND_BUS, but the observed trace expects input_axis_tready=1 at cycle 8 while the simulation produces 0. This indicates the ready signal should remain asserted from the previous cycle (cycle 7) when the output side is not yet ready to accept the next word. Preserving the register value across the IDLE→TRANSFER_IN boundary maintains back-pressure compliance without dropping ready prematurely."
