      "mechanism": "The patch adds '&& (output_axis_tready_int)' to the EXPAND_BUS guard at line 10177 (STATE_TRANSFER_OUT, EXPAND_BUS branch). When output_axis_tready_int is low, this prevents the FSM from re-entering STATE_TRANSFER_IN or STATE_IDLE and keeps it in STATE_TRANSFER_OUT, which holds input_axis_tready_next=0. At cycle 8 the trace expects input_axis_tready=1, meaning the output buffer must be ready to accept the next input word; qualifying the transition with output_axis_tready_int aligns the state machine with the observed back-pressure handshake."
