  "explanation": "The three mismatches at cycle 8 (input_axis_tready 0→1, output_axis_tlast 0→1) and cycle 9 (output_axis_tvalid 1→0) indicate a handshake timing error in the EXPAND_BUS (64→8) path. The FSM drops input_axis_tready and fails to assert output_axis_tlast when the output buffer becomes ready. The top-ranked patches (0517c5c2c927, e7dee5af7c13, 6b110907b92c) directly address the ready/valid gating in STATE_IDLE and STATE_TRANSFER_OUT for EXPAND_BUS, preserving ready across cycles and qualifying state transitions with output_axis_tready_int. The remaining patches are structurally analogous condition gates on the same static dependency cone (cycle 8, input_axis_tready) that qualify frame-boundary (tlast) and valid signals with output readiness, collectively covering the framing and back-pressure contract."
